hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19256","Waki narrated to us, Abu Hilal narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Sawadah from Anas ibn Malik, a man from Banu Abdullah ibn Kab, who said: The cavalry of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raided us. I came to him while he was eating lunch. He said: Come and eat. I said: I am fasting. He said: Sit, I will tell you about fasting. Allah has relieved the traveler of half the prayer, and the traveler, the pregnant, and the nursing of fasting. By Allah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said them both or one of them. O my regret, would that I had eaten of the food of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"19257","Affan narrated to us, he said: Abu Hilal narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Sawadah narrated to us from Anas ibn Malik, a man from Banu Abdullah ibn Kab, and he is not the Ansari, who said: The cavalry of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raided us, and he mentioned the hadith."
"19258","Abdullah said: Shayban narrated to us, Abu Hilal narrated to us, he said: He mentioned similar to it."
